# Line endings.
#
# Without this file the working tree follows each developer's core.autocrlf.
# On Windows that is CRLF, and gofmt only accepts LF — so `gofmt -l ./...`
# reported every Go file in the repository as unformatted and could never be
# used as a check. Pinning the working tree to LF makes formatting mean the
# same thing on every machine and in CI.
#
# Editors on Windows handle LF fine; the two exceptions below are file types
# that are still parsed by CRLF-only tooling.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Batch files are read by cmd.exe, which requires CRLF.
*.bat text eol=crlf
*.cmd text eol=crlf

# Binary assets: never touched, never diffed as text.
*.png binary
*.ico binary
*.exe binary
*.woff binary
*.woff2 binary

# Generated or vendored files that should not clutter a diff or a language
# breakdown.
go.sum -diff linguist-generated
fixtures/** linguist-vendored
